            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "ab7435d6fc68ceb88cf64359f87b909d54dd040bc28cb141c76d820877092931",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ab7435d6fc68-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The case concerns whether petitioner Montejo should be denied Sixth Amendment protections under Michigan v. Jackson because he silently acquiesced to the appointment of counsel rather than affirmatively accepting it."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ab7435d6fc68ceb88cf64359f87b909d54dd040bc28cb141c76d820877092931",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ab7435d6fc68-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The Louisiana Supreme Court held that an affirmative acceptance was required to trigger Jackson, and therefore upheld a confession obtained after counsel was appointed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Ms. LANDRY; Ms. Landry",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ab7435d6fc68ceb88cf64359f87b909d54dd040bc28cb141c76d820877092931",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ab7435d6fc68-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          },
          {
            "document_hash": "ab7435d6fc68ceb88cf64359f87b909d54dd040bc28cb141c76d820877092931",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ab7435d6fc68-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 31,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The parties debated whether the mere appointment of counsel satisfies the request requirement under Jackson, with arguments from Ms. Landry and others that the appointment alone should be sufficient."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ab7435d6fc68ceb88cf64359f87b909d54dd040bc28cb141c76d820877092931",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ab7435d6fc68-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked whether Michigan v. Jackson is immune from reexamination at this point."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "ab7435d6fc68ceb88cf64359f87b909d54dd040bc28cb141c76d820877092931",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-ab7435d6fc68-0002-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justices noted that if Montejo had explicitly accepted counsel at a hearing, that would satisfy Jackson and change the case outcome."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
