                "end": 21,
                "start": 20
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. VERRILLI, petitioner contends that Jackson should not be reexamined in this case because the respondent has not asked for it and a special justification is required to overrule it."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Ms. Landry",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "ab7435d6fc68ceb88cf64359f87b909d54dd040bc28cb141c76d820877092931",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-ab7435d6fc68-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 39,
                "start": 39
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Landry, petitioner asserts that the mere appointment of counsel constitutes the request necessary under Jackson to invoke the rule."
        }
      ],
